# React Query destructuring

When using `useQuery` in client components, destructure the result. Do not access `query.data` or `query.isPending` via dot notation.

## Pattern

1. Destructure `{ data, isPending }` from `useQuery(...)`.
2. Hooks that must run before the loading guard (e.g. form hooks) use `data?.field ?? default`.
3. Early return when `isPending || !data`.
4. After the guard, destructure fields from `data` for render-time values.

```tsx
const { data, isPending } = useQuery(
  orpc.getApplicationPassword.queryOptions({
    staleTime: SETTINGS_STALE_TIME_MS,
  })
);

const form = useApplicationPasswordForm(onSave, {
  password: data?.password ?? "",
});

if (isPending || !data) {
  return (
    <div className="py-6">
      <LoadingImage />
    </div>
  );
}

const { password } = data;
const hasSavedPassword = password.length > 0;
```

## Avoid

```tsx
// ❌ Dot access on query object
const passwordQuery = useQuery(...);
if (passwordQuery.isPending || !passwordQuery.data) { ... }
const password = passwordQuery.data.password;

// ❌ Split Content wrapper just to satisfy hooks — inline in one component
const FormContent = ({ password }: { password: string }) => { ... };
```

Reference: `apps/web/src/app/(protected)/(app)/(settings)/*/apply-form.tsx`, `workday-form.tsx`, `ats-form.tsx`, `integrations.tsx`.
